# Native Steam USE flags. Copied ONLY when --steam native (a standalone/full
# desktop). Steam is a 32-bit application: it needs the multilib runtime libraries
# built with ABI_X86_32. We scope ABI_X86_32 to steam-launcher's known runtime
# dependency stack rather than flipping it globally, to keep the rest of the build
# 64-bit. The builder also sets ABI_X86="64 32" in make.conf so the deps resolve.
games-util/steam-launcher -hwgfx
# steam-launcher[desktop-portal] pulls xdg-desktop-portal -> pipewire[X] ->
# media-libs/libcanberra, whose REQUIRED_USE="udev? ( alsa )" is violated by the
# profile default (udev on, alsa off). Enable alsa so the portal/sound chain
# resolves (caught on the first standalone build, blocked BOTH thin and thick).
media-libs/libcanberra alsa
media-libs/mesa abi_x86_32
media-libs/libglvnd abi_x86_32
x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers abi_x86_32
media-libs/vulkan-loader abi_x86_32
media-libs/libva abi_x86_32
virtual/opengl abi_x86_32
sys-libs/zlib abi_x86_32
